    LLM: 'Game: Texas 42. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Texas 42 is a four-player partnership trick-taking game using a double-six domino set (28 tiles). Each draws 7; bid 30â€“42 (points the team will take). High bidder names trump (blanks, 1sâ€“6s, doubles, or no-trump) and leads. Follow suit; else any tile. 42 points per hand: 1 per trick plus count tiles (5-5 and 6-4 = 10 each; 5-0, 4-1, 3-2 = 5 each). Meet bid to score; else opponents get bid plus points. First to 250 (or 7 marks) wins.',
